 "notes": "Table XV Part II 'Bi-lingualism', one opening pp. 490-491 (continued from leaf 504 to 505; header printed only on p. 490). Only Males and Females are printed (no Persons column): persons is null throughout. Rows = tahsils grouped under district (area_path = [United Provinces, district]); only tahsils where bilingualism was recorded are listed. Columns: 3-4 total returning mother tongue Bhotia, 5-6 of whom subsidiary Hindustani; 7-8 total returning mother tongue Hindustani; 9-24 of whom subsidiary Bhotia, Marathi, Oriya, Bihari, Rajasthani, Haburi, Punjabi, Nepali; 25-28 Haburi total / subsidiary Hindustani; 29-32 Kanjari; 33-36 Kanphari; 37-40 Nati. Records with subsidiary null are the 'total who returned mother-tongue X' columns (not a subsidiary language). null in males/females = printed '..' (nil); a record is emitted when at least one of the pair is printed. Page is printed sideways (rotated 90 deg clockwise to read) and slightly skewed: small figures in the right-hand columns sit up to ~20 px (about 2/3 of a row) lower than the row's figures in cols 7-8, so row placement was fixed by measuring baselines and counting row-dot clusters (work/blobs.py) rather than by eye alone. No totals are printed in this table (no district/province total rows), so the only arithmetic checks are subsidiary <= total for each mother tongue (all pass). 49 tahsil rows, Dehra Dun to Etawah; continues on leaf 505. Printed district name 'Moerut' read as Meerut (broken type; tahsil 'Meerut' same). Tahsil 'Mustafabad * (Jasrana).' printed over two lines."
